# L §4.2 "A day not yet fixed", §2.3 `cday` (tally 2.3, #247; G3): a day in a calendar's `added` is a day or
# a hole; a window there is refused at load, `LOAD-PARSE`, with the forms that say it (one day in a row
# marked `assumed`, or an axis keying the calendar). Before: `window(2026-05-05, 2026-05-06)`.
=== m.tally
model addedw
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
input cal: calendar
input d: date
input n: int
version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [window(2026-05-04, 2026-05-06)]) "c"
  d = 2026-05-01 "c"
  n = 2 "c"
ask a: add_business(d, n, cal)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: a window in added; added takes a day or a hole: state one day in a row marked assumed, or key the calendar by an axis (m.tally:14)
